  "_comment": [
    "The words a caller actually says, per knowledge topic.",
    "",
    "Bland's retrieval is closer to lexical than semantic. Verified against the live",
    "base: the query '43 feet' retrieves the ceiling entry perfectly, while 'How high",
    "are the ceilings?' retrieves nothing at all and the agent tells the caller it",
    "does not have that information. That happened on the first real test call.",
    "",
    "Short entries suffer most, because there are barely any words in them to match",
    "against. So every entry likely to be asked in words that differ from its topic",
    "gets its phrasings listed here, and the sync writes them into the document as",
    "an 'Also asked as' line.",
    "",
    "Keyed by the EXACT topic string from Kumi, or from knowledge-supplement.json.",
    "A key that matches no entry is harmless, so these can be written ahead of the",
    "row existing."
